 "history": "On the Gambia and the Gold Coast men wore a cloth of narrow-strip cotton wrapped round the waist to the knee, often indigo and white, the better-off a longer and finer one; in Kongo raffia panels sewn side by side. The same plain rectangle, told apart by its cloth, was the Yemeni futa, the South Indian lungi and the Malay sarong worn over drawers [AF-A2][AF-C3][NIE][SA7][ML1].",
